/**
 * @page reference Reference guide
 *
 * The application API lives in llamad::client: start with llamad::client::Client,
 * llamad::client::ToolSet and the checked conversions in llamad::client::json.
 * The daemon combines llamad::Engine, llamad::ChatFormat and llamad::LlamaService.
 * Command-line parsing lives in llamad::cli and wire conversion in llamad::wire.
 *
 * Only llamad-owned sources are indexed. Vendored llama.cpp, generated protobuf
 * sources and test fixtures are outside the API reference. The executable examples
 * are included in the source browser; tests are described on @ref testing.
 *
 * @see wire_contract
 * @see testing
 */

/**
 * @page wire_contract Wire contract
 *
 * The daemon exposes `llamad.v1.Llama` on a mode-0600 Unix domain socket. Requests
 * contain their entire history and tool definitions; the server keeps no sessions
 * and executes no tools. LlamaService translates requests to plain engine and chat
 * types. The client presents the same contract without exposing protobuf types.
 *
 * Successful generation streams end with exactly one final chunk carrying statistics
 * and a finish reason. Transport errors or client cancellation can end a stream before
 * that chunk. Tool calls are atomic and appear only on the final chunk with TOOL_CALLS.
 * Embed returns one L2-normalised vector per input and is served only by an embedding
 * model, which in turn serves no generation. Caller errors map to INVALID_ARGUMENT, a
 * missing capability (no usable chat template, or the wrong kind of model for the RPC)
 * to FAILED_PRECONDITION, and other failures to INTERNAL.
 *
 * Doxygen has no Protocol Buffers parser. The authoritative, commented schema is
 * included verbatim so message fields, numbers and defaults stay tied to the source.
 * @verbinclude proto/llamad/v1/llamad.proto
 */

/**
 * @page testing Tests and executable examples
 *
 * CTest runs model-free executable tests: chat_format_test.cpp checks real template
 * rendering and canned tool output; flags_test.cpp checks reflected options;
 * contract_test.cpp checks both directions of every wire mirror; json_test.cpp and
 * client_tools_test.cpp check conversion, schema generation and dispatch;
 * client_chat_test.cpp scripts a fake service on a private Unix socket to check the
 * client tool loop and embed call.
 *
 * client/examples/chat_cli.cpp demonstrates streaming chat, reflected tools and embeddings.
 * tests/engine_smoke.cpp exercises raw generation, grammar constraints, cancellation,
 * chat rendering and embeddings in-process. It needs a local GGUF model and is not a CTest test.
 * tests/engine_bench.cpp measures prefill and decode tokens per second the same way; see
 * docs/performance.md.
 * docs/building.md describes the build, test and smoke-test scripts.
 */
